  "notes": "USAGE:\nA strong, formal word typically used in public discourse, policy, and media. Implies total and permanent elimination, not just reduction.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {根絶|こんぜつ}する (to eradicate)\n- {根絶|こんぜつ}を{目指|めざ}す (to aim for eradication)\n- {病気|びょうき}の{根絶|こんぜつ} (eradication of disease)\n- {根絶|こんぜつ}やし (completely wiping out — emphatic colloquial form)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {撲滅|ぼくめつ}: eradication; stamping out — similar strength, often used for crime, drugs, and social evils\n- {排除|はいじょ}: exclusion; removal — less absolute, means removing rather than completely destroying",
